{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Wondering.</b> Astonished at the abundance of her alacrity to perform kindness." "<b>Kept silent.</b> And did not say to her, 'Do not exert yourself so much,' as would have been proper according to the law of ethics — so as to know and recognize from the manner of her piety and alacrity." "<b>Whether YHWH had made his way prosperous.</b> Whether it would be in the direction of the good and perfect kindness." "<b>Or not.</b> And whether all this would be for the hope of some reward."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:23.987900418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}